[MODULE] Decoder RNN (brain3/fuzzy/decoder.hpp)
[LAYER]  C++ Neural Core (Language Generation)
[TYPE]   Autoregressive Sequence-to-Sequence RNN

[DEEP ARCHITECTURE & MECHANICS]
The `decoder.hpp` file implements a lightweight, native C++ Elman Recurrent Neural Network (RNN). It is used to convert abstract, geometric "concept vectors" generated by the Brains Imagination/Reasoning engines into human-readable sequential English words.

1. The Neural Architecture:
   - Hidden State Update: `h_next = tanh(W_ih * x_t + W_hh * h_prev + b_h)`
   - Output Projection: `y_t = W_ho * h_next + b_o`
   
2. Autoregressive Generation:
   The `generate()` function takes an initial 64D concept vector as a seed. It feeds it into the RNN to predict the first word. It then feeds the output vector *back into the input* of the RNN to predict the next word, chaining them together until it hits a maximum length or predicts a "HALT" token.

[SUMMARY]
It is the "Mouth" of the C++ fuzzy layer. It translates abstract, high-dimensional thought geometries into sequential language tokens without relying on a massive external LLM.

