[MODULE] Symbolic Factorizer (brain3/crisp/factorizer.hpp)
[LAYER]  C++ Crisp Core
[TYPE]   S-Expression Evaluator

[DEEP ARCHITECTURE & MECHANICS]
A lightning-fast, native C++ S-expression parser. When the Python reasoning engine factors a complex equation (e.g., `x^2 + 2x + 1` to `(x + 1)^2`), it sends the symbolic trees to C++ as S-expressions like `(* (+ x 1) (+ x 1))`. 
This module parses the tree and evaluates it against random variable environments (`map<string, double>`) in C++ to mathematically prove that the two expressions are identical, instantly validating the Python logic.

