[MODULE] Invariant Miner (brain3/crisp/invariants.hpp)
[LAYER]  C++ Crisp Core
[TYPE]   Logical Pre-Filter

[DEEP ARCHITECTURE & MECHANICS]
This is a native C++ port of the Python invariant miner. When synthesizing code or logic, it is incredibly expensive to run every candidate through a full oracle or unit test. 
This module looks at the input/output examples and automatically deduces "Invariants" (e.g., `out_nonneg` -> the output is always positive, or `out_ge_max_arg` -> the output is always greater than or equal to the largest input). 
It uses these mathematical invariants as a lightning-fast pre-filter to instantly reject hallucinated code before wasting compute on a full test.

