[MODULE] Language / Inner Speech (brain3/fuzzy/language.hpp)
[LAYER]  C++ Neural/Fuzzy Core
[TYPE]   Hebbian Word Embedding Space

[DEEP ARCHITECTURE & MECHANICS]
The `language.hpp` module maps discrete human words to continuous geometric concept vectors, allowing the Brain to actually "understand" what words mean visually/spatially.

1. No Hardcoded Grammar:
   There are no grammar rules or templates. Words are just vectors in the exact same mathematical space as visual perceptions.
   
2. Hebbian Learning (Meaning through Co-occurrence):
   When the Brain hears a word, it looks at what the SOM (Visual cortex) is currently seeing. It mathematically pulls the words vector slightly closer to the SOMs current vector (`word_vec += lr * (som_activation - word_vec)`).
   Over time, the word "Dog" physically drifts to the same location in high-dimensional space as the visual representation of a Dog.

3. SIMD Fast Decoding:
   To speak, the Brain takes a concept vector and finds the closest word. It uses a `flat_embeddings_` matrix for blazing-fast sequential memory access during cosine similarity checks.

[SUMMARY]
This module bridges the gap between raw neural geometry and discrete language by anchoring words directly to perceptual experiences.

